/**
 * @mainpage DspCore
 * @version 0.2.0
 *
 * DspCore is the signal-processing layer of the RoModular ecosystem: lookup
 * tables, interpolation, generators, filters, dynamics, analysis and
 * transforms for desktop and embedded targets, built on Foundation.
 *
 * @note Development includes LUT storage, interpolation, generators, filters and analysis; further features follow
 * `ACTION_PLAN.md`.
 *
 * @section DspCoreMainModules Modules
 *
 * The complete API is organized under **Topics**. **Classes** lists state and storage
 * types; stateless functions appear in their module topics.
 *
 * - @ref DspCore_Filters "Filters": single-rate FIR/IIR processors and Biquad coefficient calculators.
 * - @ref DspCore_Dynamics "Dynamics": planned signal-dependent processors.
 * - @ref DspCore_Analysis "Analysis": implemented peak/RMS plus planned response and pole-zero analysis.
 * - @ref DspCore_Transforms "Transforms": planned DFT/FFT implementations.
 * - @ref DspCore_Generators "Generators": periodic, shaping, envelopes, noise and windows.
 * - @ref DspCore_Interpolation "Interpolation": linear, bilinear and trilinear formulas.
 * - @ref DspCore_LUT "Lookup tables": 1D, 2D and 3D arithmetic storage plus sampled access.
 * - @ref DspCore_Core "Core": DspCore and Foundation version information.
 *
 * - @ref DspCore_Architecture "Architecture and planned content".
 * - @ref DspCore_Numeric "Numeric and buffer contracts".
 *
 * @section DspCoreMainDependency Dependencies
 *
 * DspCore links `Foundation::Foundation` (Foundation 2.0 or a newer 2.x
 * release, built on CPSTL). It uses local
 * packages when available and otherwise fetches the pinned release from
 * GitHub; see @ref DspCore_BuildGuide_Dependency.
 */
